       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1000 mg is five times the maximum recommended sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **100 mg** once daily, which is a typical dose for depression, anxiety, or similar indications.\n- **50 mg** once daily, which is the usual starting dose for depression, GAD, and PTSD. For panic disorder, PTSD, or social anxiety, the starting dose is often 25 mg.\n- **200 mg** once daily, which is the maximum.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1000 mg, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd enter it only with that confirmation and a note on the order, and pharmacy will probably want to verify it."
